  "meta": {
    "about": "GridCraft → CadCraft → VectorCraft. The beds live in a spreadsheet (position, size), which also works out the area, the soil each bed needs at 30 cm deep and how many 50-litre bags of compost to buy. GridCraft computes each bed's corners, CadCraft draws them inside the fence as a dimensioned plan, and VectorCraft turns the drawing into a friendly hand-drawn plan to stick on the shed door. Move a bed in the spreadsheet and the plan follows.",
    "tags": [
      "garden",
      "planning",
      "data-to-drawing"
    ],
    "title": "Garden planner: from a spreadsheet to a plan"
  },
